## Analysis

**Experiments with valid Elastic Modulus measurements:**
1. 17 wt%, 25°C mix, 5°C bath, 10 mm/s, N2, 30s wait, 1200s → **547.2 MPa** (CV=0.112, fit quality 58/100, 1 discarded)
2. 18 wt%, 80°C mix, 15°C bath, 15 mm/s, no N2, 600s wait, 1350s → **476.8 MPa** (CV=0.091, fit quality 0/100, 1 discarded)
3. 17 wt%, 35°C mix, 10°C bath, 20 mm/s, no N2, 90s wait, 1400s → **401.3 MPa** (CV=0.012, fit quality 29/100, 2 discarded)
4. 17.5 wt%, 55°C mix, 25°C bath, 11 mm/s, N2, 375s wait, 1300s → **591.7 MPa** (CV=0.109, fit quality 54.5/100, 2 discarded)
5. 18 wt%, 30°C mix, 20°C bath, 16 mm/s, N2, 500s wait, 1450s → **400.0 MPa** (CV=nan, fit quality 38/100, 3 discarded)

**Experiments with no valid modulus (all fits failed):** 21 wt%, 19 wt%, 20 wt%, 18.5 wt%, 19.5 wt%, 20.5 wt%

**Key observations:**
- Best validated modulus: 591.7 MPa (17.5 wt%, 55°C mix, 25°C bath, N2, 375s wait, 1300s)
- Second best: 547.2 MPa (17 wt%, 25°C mix, 5°C bath, N2, 30s wait, 1200s)
- Higher polymer concentrations (19–21 wt%) consistently fail to produce measurable modulus
- Lower polymer concentrations (17–18.5 wt%) tend to yield measurable modulus
- Warm bath (25°C) + N2 + moderate wait appears favorable (experiment 4)

**Explore mode — sparse regions to cover:**
- bath_temp=5°C has been heavily sampled; bath_temp=25°C has only 2 samples (one failed, one best result)
- mixing_temp around 25–35°C with bath_temp=25°C is sparse
- polymer_wt ~17–18 wt% with bath_temp=25°C and short wait is underexplored
- nips_bath_wait_time near 1800s with bath_temp=25°C is unexplored
- pullcast_speed ~8–9 mm/s with these conditions is novel

A combination of: polymer_wt=17.5, mixing_temp=25°C, bath_temp=25°C, pullcast_speed=9 mm/s, N2=True, wait=120s, nips_bath_wait_time=1800s would be genuinely novel — low mixing temp (sparse at 25°C outside the max-polymer constraint), warm bath, short-moderate wait, longer immersion, and a pullcast speed not yet used.

