## Analysis

**Validated modulus results (reliable fits, measured values):**
- 17.5 wt%, mixing_temp=55°C, bath_temp=25°C, speed=11, N2=True, wait=375s, nips=1300s → **591.7 MPa** (CV=0.109, fit quality 54.5/100, 2 discarded)
- 17 wt%, mixing_temp=25°C, bath_temp=5°C, speed=10, N2=True, wait=30s, nips=1200s → **547.2 MPa** (CV=0.112, fit quality 58/100, 1 discarded)
- 17.5 wt%, mixing_temp=25°C, bath_temp=25°C, speed=9, N2=True, wait=120s, nips=1800s → **494.6 MPa** (CV=0.176, membrane defects)
- 18 wt%, mixing_temp=80°C, bath_temp=15°C, speed=15, N2=False, wait=600s, nips=1350s → **476.8 MPa**
- 17 wt%, mixing_temp=35°C, bath_temp=10°C, speed=20, N2=False, wait=90s, nips=1400s → **401.3 MPa**
- 18 wt%, mixing_temp=30°C, bath_temp=20°C, speed=16, N2=True, wait=500s, nips=1450s → **400.0 MPa**

**No valid modulus:** 21 wt% (failed fits), 19 wt%, 20 wt%, 18.5 wt%, 19.5 wt%, 20.5 wt% — all had 100% discarded fits.

**Key observations:**
- Lower polymer concentrations (17–17.5 wt%) consistently yield the best modulus
- N2 purge appears beneficial for top performers
- Bath temp=25°C with N2 appears in two top performers
- The 17.5 wt% / 55°C / bath=25°C / N2 result is the current best but has moderate CV and fit quality — not yet independently validated
- Sparse region: mixing_temp ~65°C, bath_temp ~10°C, polymer_wt ~17–17.5, short wait, moderate speed

**Explore mode directive:** Propose a deliberately novel point far from existing conditions. Underrepresented combinations include: low polymer wt (~17–17.5) + intermediate bath temp (~10°C) + intermediate mixing temp (~65°C) + short wait + N2 + nips_bath_wait_time near max. The combination of mixing_temp=65°C, bath_temp=10°C, polymer_wt=17.5, N2=True, short wait (~15s), speed=6 mm/s, nips=1800s is genuinely novel and distant from all sampled points.

