**Key observations:**
- Best result: 17.5wt%, 65°C mix, **10°C bath**, 6mm/s, N2, 15s wait, 1800s → 708.9 MPa
- Second best: 17.5wt%, 55°C mix, **25°C bath**, 11mm/s, N2, 375s wait → 591.7 MPa
- Many experiments with no modulus (all fits failed): 19wt%, 19.5wt%, 20wt%, 20.5wt%, 21wt% — higher polymer concentrations consistently fail to yield reliable fits
- Lower polymer concentrations (17–17.5wt%) with N2, cold bath, moderate-high mixing temp appear favorable

**Coverage gaps for exploration:**
- `bath_temp` = 5°C has been heavily sampled; 10°C has 2 points; 15°C has 1; 20°C has 1; 25°C has 3
- `mixing_temp` around 65–75°C with **bath_temp ~10°C** and **low polymer_wt** is promising but sparse
- `nips_bath_wait_time` at 1800s with bath_temp=10°C only has the best result (65°C mix)
- `pullcast_speed` ~14–17mm/s with N2 and low polymer_wt is underexplored
- `coupon_to_bath_wait_time` very short (0–30s) with N2 and 10°C bath is sparse beyond the best result

**Explore mode reasoning:**
The best result used: 17.5wt%, 65°C mix, 10°C bath, 6mm/s, N2, 15s, 1800s. To explore a genuinely novel region while informed by this signal, I'll target:
- Similar low polymer_wt (17.5wt%) and N2 
- Higher mixing temp (75°C — between 65 and 80, undersampled)
- bath_temp = 10°C (only 2 points here, both good)
- Higher pullcast_speed (~14mm/s — sparse in this combination)
- Short wait time (~45s — between 15s and 90s, sparse)
- nips_bath_wait_time = 1550s (undersampled mid-range)

This is genuinely far from all prior points in the combined parameter space.

